    "comment": "A footprint (source) that continues another neuron's track (target) better than its own: closer than 2·(σ_det + σ_move) of the fitted model to that neuron's previous or next detection, but farther from its own neuron's. The other neuron has a footprint in this session too, so the two may be swapped (without one: misassigned / orphans). Union distances do not matter — drift and fluctuations can bring two tracks close in single sessions. Review both neurons; exchange the footprints by reassigning (the occupied slot is asked for).",
